      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 784,
        "content": "## Scrape Blog Posts with Firecrawl and Save to Google Docs\n\n### How it works\n\n1. Manually triggers a batch scrape of a list of blog post URLs via Firecrawl.\n2. Waits 1 minute, then polls Firecrawl for the batch scrape status.\n3. Repeats the wait-and-check loop until the scrape job reports completed or failed.\n4. Stops with a clear error if the scrape job fails, instead of polling indefinitely.\n5. Creates a new Google Doc once the scrape finishes.\n6. Cleans the scraped markdown (strips nav/footer, links, and formatting) in a Code node.\n7. Inserts the cleaned text into the Google Doc.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- [ ] Add a Firecrawl API credential and select it on both Firecrawl nodes.\n- [ ] Add Google Docs OAuth2 credentials and select them on both Google Docs nodes.\n- [ ] Replace the hardcoded URL list in \"Batch Scrape Blog Post URLs\" with your own target URLs.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the wait duration or the footer marker text in \"Clean Scraped Markdown\" to match a different source site. Network calls (Firecrawl, Google Docs) retry up to 3 times on transient failure."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "6e48425a-d11b-4459-8059-a2bc5f9e6a1c",
      "name": "Sticky Note5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
